  "body": "Small findings of the post audit against the SINUMERIK manuals (#4130). None changes a toolpath.\n\n1. 840D: the preamble writes no `G94` (`assets/posts/sinumerik.cps:501`). The 810M post does (`sinumerik-810m.cps:429`). A reset normally restores `G94`.\n2. 810M: `L84` with `R08=-3` is called rigid tapping by default (`sinumerik-810m.cps:26`, `:751-762`). The cited EMCO text says `L84` needs a compensating chuck, with or without an encoder. Correct the operator note and check the Siemens text.\n\nEvidence: upstream/main `f0bdc5109`.\n\nDone means: each item is fixed with a test, or closed with a reason in a comment.\n",
